Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: pin S16_LE on the qrb4210-rb2 card

qforge, 2026-10-09. Replaces ROCKNIX SM6115 0037 ("constrain BE format mask to S16_LE only"),
which forced 16-bit on every stream of every board the sm8250 machine driver serves. That
collides with 0870 (Nova-Deck; also ROCKNIX SM8250 0100), which deliberately lets non-compressed
streams negotiate on the SM8250 boards. Both are right for their boards, so the strict rule is
scoped to the card compatible the MANGMI Air X uses: qcom,qrb4210-rb2-sndcard. On it the ES8326
headphone codec and AW88261 amps sit on MI2S and take 16-bit only, and adding S16_LE to the mask
(what 0870 keeps doing for compressed streams) is not enough -- the front end can still pick
S32_LE -- hence params_set_format().

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dapm.h>
@@ -67,8 +68,16 @@
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
 
-	/* Only force S16_LE format for compressed playback */
-	if (rtd->dai_link->compr_ops) {
+	/*
+	 * Only force S16_LE format for compressed playback -- except on the
+	 * qrb4210-rb2 card (SM6115, MANGMI Air X): its ES8326 and AW88261 MI2S
+	 * back ends take 16-bit only, and merely adding S16_LE to the mask still
+	 * lets the front end negotiate S32_LE, so pin the format outright there.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(rtd->card->dev->of_node,
+				    "qcom,qrb4210-rb2-sndcard")) {
+		params_set_format(params, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+	} else if (rtd->dai_link->compr_ops) {
 		/* This is a compressed stream, set format to S16_LE */
 		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
 	} else {
